message.content:
{
  "answer_markdown": "To fetch live data from a connected tool like Gmail, Drive, or Notion in Mistral's Work chat, you should use the **Connectors** feature. This allows Work to securely retrieve, analyze, and act on data from these services without you needing to switch between apps.\n\n### How to Use Connectors\n1. Click the `+` icon or type `/` in the chat window.\n2. Select `Tools` then enable the Connector you want to use.\n\nExample prompt:\n```\n\"Find the latest Q3 revenue deck in Google Drive and prepare a one-page summary.\"\n```\n\nConnectors differ from **Web Search** in that:\n- **Connectors** pull live, structured data from specific tools (Gmail, Drive, Notion) that you have already connected and authenticated.\n- **Web Search** fetches up-to-date information from the open web but does not integrate with external tools or provide structured, cited reports.\n\nTo enable a Connector:\n```\n1. Click the `+` icon or type `/` in the chat window.\n2. Select `Tools` then enable the Connector you want to use.\n```\n\nWork will then decide which Connector to call based on your request and ask for authentication if needed. It also provides approval prompts before sensitive actions, ensuring transparency and control.\n\nFor more details, see [Using Connectors in tasks](https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/work/connectors#using-connectors) [4].",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "Pick the option that fits your situation:"
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "quote": "Connectors are secure bridges between Work and your external tools and data sources."
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "quote": "Once connected, Work can use the Connector automatically when relevant."
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "quote": "Click the `+` icon or type `/` in the chat window."
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "quote": "Select `Tools` then enable the Connector you want to use."
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

