message.content:
{
  "answer_markdown": "To hand off your work from a terminal session to a cloud session in Vibe Code Web, use the `/teleport` command from the Mistral CLI. This moves your active local session into a Vibe Code Web sandbox, allowing you to continue your work in the cloud without keeping your terminal open.\n\n```bash\n/teleport\n```\n\nBy teleporting to Vibe Code Web, you give up the following:\n- **Local filesystem and shell access**: The session runs in a remote sandbox, so you no longer have direct access to your local files or shell. [2]\n- **Non-interactive mode**: The cloud session does not support non-interactive mode, unlike the CLI. [2]\n- **Local model flexibility**: The cloud session runs on Mistral Medium 3.5, regardless of the local model you were using. [7]\n- **One-way operation**: Once teleported, you cannot pull the session back into the local CLI. [7]\n\nThe cloud session will typically clone your repository, work through the task, and push a branch with a draft pull request when done. [7]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "The CLI is the most flexible surface. It runs in any terminal emulator, supports interactive sessions and scripting, and has full access to your shell and working tree."
    },
    {
      "n": 7,
      "quote": "Commits, branches, and pull requests created during the run stay in your repository. The sandbox is deleted when the session ends."
    },
    {
      "n": 7,
      "quote": "Teleport is one-way. Once a session moves to the cloud, you can't pull it back into the local CLI. Continue from Vibe Code Web."
    },
    {
      "n": 7,
      "quote": "Cloud sessions run on Mistral Medium 3.5, regardless of the local model."
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

