  "answer_markdown": "When you set the `VIBE_HOME` environment variable for the Mistral CLI, the following files and subdirectories move to the new location:\n\n- `config.toml`: main configuration\n- `.env`: API keys and provider credentials\n- `agents/`: custom agent profiles\n- `prompts/`: custom system prompts\n- `skills/`: custom skills\n- `tools/`: custom tools\n- `logs/`: session and application logs\n\n```bash\nexport VIBE_HOME=\"\\/path\\/to\\/custom\\/vibe\\/home\"\n```\n\nAdditionally, the `AGENTS.md` file, which is used to follow project-specific agent instructions, is also affected by the `VIBE_HOME` environment variable if it is located in the user-level directory [5].",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "By default, the CLI stores its configuration and state in `~/.vibe/`. Override the location with the `VIBE_HOME` environment variable:"
