message.content:
{
  "answer_markdown": "The `GET /v1/files/{file_id}/content` operation in Mistral AI's Files API requires the `file_id` parameter, which must be a UUID string and is required in the path. On success, it returns the raw content of the file as a binary stream with the MIME type `application/octet-stream` [1].\n\nTo download a file, you can use the following cURL command:\n\n```bash\ncurl --location \"https://api.mistral.ai/v1/files/<file_id>/content\" \\\n     --header 'Accept: application/octet-stream' \\\n     --header 'Accept-Encoding: gzip, deflate, zstd' \\\n     --header \"Authorization: Bearer $MISTRAL_API_KEY\"\n```\n\nOr in Python, you can use the `client.files.download` method:\n\n```python\nfile_bytes = client.files.download(file_id=file_chunk.file_id).read()\n\n# Save the file locally\nwith open(f\"image_generated.png\", \"wb\") as file:\n    file.write(file_bytes)\n```",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "Operation id: `files_api_routes_download_file` - Tag: files"
    },
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "### Responses\n- `200` — OK (application/octet-stream)"
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "quote": "curl --location \"https://api.mistral.ai/v1/files/<file_id>/content\" \\"
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "quote": "file_bytes = client.files.download(file_id=file_chunk.file_id).read()"
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

